counterfactuals.output:
1. A fluid-filled engine mount comprising:  
a first mounting member and a second mounting member;  
an elastic body elastically connecting the first mounting member to the second mounting member;  
a fluid chamber containing a non-compressible fluid;  
a rigid partition member dividing the fluid chamber into a pressure-receiving chamber and an equilibrium chamber; and  
an annular elastic partition component disposed adjacent to the rigid partition member,  
wherein a contact surface of the annular elastic partition component directly abuts a corresponding surface of the rigid partition member while remaining unbonded thereto.
